# Configurable keybindings

When adding or changing keybindings in lnav-rs:

- Wire them through `[keys]` and/or `[details_keys]` (see `src/keys.rs` defaults), not hardcoded intercepts in input handlers.
- Hardcode only rare exceptions that already exist for structural reasons (e.g. Esc closing details, `:` / `q` leaving overlay focus) — do not add new hardcoded action keys.
- Prefer context via `[details_keys]` overlays when list and details need different bindings for the same key.
- Document new bindings in the README key tables and example `[keys]` / `[details_keys]` snippets.
